ilding  for eight years before coach Popovich  gave her that opportunity I've been  around you know when I'm around the  league and players are coming up to me  in pregame and they're like hey you know  I'd like you to meet my family or can  you meet my girlfriend or my my mom or  you're going into practice and they're  like hey hall-of-famer or legend I kept  telling Ron Butler don't do that because  the guys next to me we're all just  assistant coaches and I'm I cannot take  away Who I am  you hired me and you knew who I was but  I have to also fit in with my brothers  and when you have great advocate like  blah Dee Dee vod's and the backhand and  rick carlisle the president of the the  NBA coaches association you have amazing  advocates that are confident enough to  know that the future is right here with  some people including women do you think  that Popovich is going to set the stage  for Becky Hammon to take over for him I  do I do they have a amazing relationship  this is just my opinion but I think that  Becky is being tutored for success and  he does have a very unique set of  circumstances even even  greater than mine and you know the same  thing with Natalie she's it with the  Clippers  you know she's worked really hard to  gain the trust and the belief of Doc  Rivers our situation in Sacramento is a  little bit you know more fluid because  different coaches it could be a little  bit more difficult for me but that's  okay we just need one and you don't  remember when Becky got the job a couple  years ago and she called me and she was  like man I'm sorry and I'm like shut up  don't be sorry you know she was she was  showing me respect as our friends and as  someone you know who you know she said  had been you know a trailblazer  we're not in a competition we just have  to you know if Jackie Robinson becomes  the first we have failed if nobody else  comes after I'm okay being Larry Doby  I'm okay with being the second but we  need more and they're out ther